<div class="calc-page">
  <div class="calc-page__header">
    <h1>Where the Money Goes</h1>
    <p>One conventional loan, followed from the bond buyer to the borrower: what moves at funding, what moves every month, and how points, comp, servicing value and the wholesaler's margin fit together. Change any input and both charts recompute.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="calc-page__body">
    <div class="wtmg">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="wtmg-head">
          <p class="note" role="note"><strong>Training tool.</strong> Every figure here is hypothetical and for illustration only. It is not a rate quote, an offer, or terms for any borrower. See the full disclosure at the bottom of the page.</p>
          <div class="key" aria-label="Color key">
            <span><i class="sw blue"></i>Blue = where money starts</span>
            <span><i class="sw green"></i>Green = where it lands</span>
            <span><i class="sw gray"></i>Gray (dashed) = estimated, not cash</span>
            <span><i class="sw yellow"></i>Yellow = keep in mind</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <form class="inputs-wrap" id="inputs" aria-label="Loan inputs" autocomplete="off">
          <div class="topbar">
            <div class="program" data-fields="program"></div>
            <div class="solve">
              <label for="in-solve">Solve for</label>
              <select id="in-solve" aria-describedby="src-solve"><option value="margin">Wholesaler margin</option><option value="msr">Servicing value</option><option value="comp">Broker comp</option><option value="price">MBS price</option><option value="sheet">Borrower points</option><option value="none">Nothing, show gap</option></select>
              <span class="s" id="src-solve">So modeled price = sheet</span>
            </div>
            <div class="resultchip"><span class="k">Borrower price</span><span class="v" id="in-result"></span></div>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="reset">Reset to example</button>
          </div>

          <%# Input cells are rendered from FIELD_DEFS in where-the-money-goes.js; each grid lists its field ids in order. %>
          <details class="sec" open>
            <summary>Loan, borrower and market</summary>
            <div class="grid" data-fields="loan propertyValue creditScore rate sheet coupon price tsy"></div>
            <div class="llpa-row" id="llpaRow">
              <div class="grid" data-fields="llpaMode llpa"></div>
              <button type="button" class="btn" id="llpaOpen" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="llpaDialog">Pick from the LLPA table</button>
            </div>
            <div class="llpa" id="llpaPanel" aria-live="polite"></div>
            <p class="hint llpa-na" id="llpaNa" hidden>FHA, VA and USDA loans carry no Fannie Mae loan-level price adjustments. Their risk pricing is the program's upfront and annual fee, shown under Assumptions and in both charts.</p>
            <details class="after" id="after">
              <summary>After lock: market move (optional)</summary>
              <div class="grid" data-fields="coupon2 price2"></div>
              <p class="hint">Once the loan is locked, type where the coupon or price moved to. The borrower's price, the comp, and the servicing mark stay fixed, so the wholesaler's margin recalculates. Changing the note rate starts a new lock and clears the move.</p>
            </details>
          </details>

          <details class="sec" open>
            <summary>Wholesaler: margin and servicing</summary>
            <div class="grid" data-fields="margin msr msrMult"></div>
          </details>

          <details class="sec" open>
            <summary>MSFG: comp</summary>
            <div class="grid" data-fields="comp lo"></div>
          </details>

          <details class="sec" id="assumptions">
            <summary>Assumptions: fixed by program, sourced, or illustrative</summary>
            <p class="hint">Servicing strip and agency fee are set by the program.</p>
            <div class="grid" data-fields="svc gfee"></div>
            <div class="fees" id="feesBlock">
              <div class="cards" id="feeCards"></div>
              <div class="grid" id="miGrid" data-fields="pmi"></div>
              <div class="fees" id="govFees" hidden>
                <div class="grid checks" data-fields="financeUpfront"></div>
                <div class="grid checks" id="vaChecks" data-fields="vaSubsequentUse vaExempt" hidden></div>
                <p class="hint">FHA annual MIP uses the 30-year bands by LTV and base loan size (0.50% / 0.55% up to $726,200; 0.70% / 0.75% above); 15-year terms differ. The VA funding fee covers purchase loans by use and down payment; IRRRL and cash-out tiers are not modeled. Rates as understood on the date in the disclosure.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="hint">Where MSFG's share of the comp goes after the LO (illustrative shares).</p>
            <div class="grid" data-fields="fixed variable onetime profit"></div>
            <details class="after" id="wsplitSec">
              <summary>Optional: what the wholesaler keeps has to cover</summary>
              <div class="grid checks" data-fields="wsplit"></div>
              <div class="grid wide" data-fields="wfixed wvariable wonetime wrate wprofit"></div>
              <p class="hint">Illustrative shares. No wholesaler publishes a per-loan cost structure; turn this on to show that the margin is gross, not profit, and edit the shares for the discussion.</p>
            </details>
          </details>

          <p class="warn" id="warnings" hidden></p>

          <%# LLPA popout: the Fannie base grid plus the borrower and property inputs that feed it. Outside the sections so a collapsed section cannot hide it. %>
          <dialog class="llpa-dialog" id="llpaDialog" aria-labelledby="llpaDialogTitle">
            <div class="llpa-dialog-head">
              <h3 id="llpaDialogTitle">Fannie Mae LLPA matrix</h3>
              <button type="button" class="btn" id="llpaClose">Done</button>
            </div>
            <p class="llpa-head" id="llpaDialogHead" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <div class="grid" data-fields="purpose occupancy units"></div>
            <p class="hint" id="llpaCaption"></p>
            <div class="llpa-scroll" id="llpaTable"></div>
            <div class="grid checks" data-fields="isCondo isManufacturedHome isHighBalance hasSubordinateFinancing applyMMI isHighLTVRefi waiverHomeReady waiverFirstTimeHB waiverDutyToServe"></div>
          </dialog>
        </form>

        <section aria-labelledby="s1">
          <h2 id="s1">At funding: the whole front end.</h2>
          <div class="cards" id="pricing"></div>
          <div class="cards" id="move" hidden></div>
          <div class="chart-scroll"><svg id="chart1" role="group" aria-label="Sankey chart of one-time flows at funding"></svg></div>
          <p class="swipe">Swipe sideways to see the full flow.</p>
          <div class="info" id="info1" role="status" aria-live="polite">Hover or tap a ribbon to see how it's calculated.</div>
          <div class="notes" id="notes1"></div>
          <div class="box">
            <h3>Where the wholesaler's front-end revenue comes from</h3>
            <div class="cards" id="rev"></div>
            <p id="revline"></p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="s2">
          <h2 id="s2">Every month: the borrower's payment.</h2>
          <p class="subhead" id="sub2"></p>
          <div class="chart-scroll"><svg id="chart2" role="group" aria-label="Sankey chart of the month-one principal and interest payment"></svg></div>
          <p class="swipe">Swipe sideways to see the full flow.</p>
          <div class="info" id="info2" role="status" aria-live="polite">Hover or tap a ribbon to see how it's calculated.</div>
          <div class="notes" id="notes2"></div>
        </section>

        <div class="boxes">
          <div class="box">
            <h3>Retained servicing: an asset, not extra cash</h3>
            <div class="cards" id="msrcards"></div>
            <p>Don't add the MSR value and future servicing income together; that counts the same money twice.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="box">
            <h3>Risks to watch</h3>
            <div class="cards">
              <div class="card y"><span class="v">Rates rise: MBS prices fall, loans last longer</span></div>
              <div class="card y"><span class="v">Early payoff / refi: premium and servicing income cut short</span></div>
              <div class="card y"><span class="v">Pipeline risk: locks, hedges, funding costs, fallout</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wtmg-foot" id="disclosure" role="contentinfo">
          <p><strong>Training and educational use only.</strong> This tool illustrates how the pricing, compensation, and servicing economics of a conventional mortgage fit together. All figures, including the example defaults and anything you enter, are hypothetical and for illustration. They are not a rate quote, a Loan Estimate, an offer, an approval, or a commitment to lend, and they are not specific to any borrower, property, or loan program.</p>
          <p>Actual rates, prices, fees, compensation, and investor execution depend on the borrower's credit profile, the loan characteristics, market conditions, and the lender, and they change without notice. Nothing on this page is financial, investment, legal, or tax advice. Mountain State Financial Group, LLC makes no representation or warranty as to the accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of any figure shown and accepts no liability for any decision made in reliance on this tool. Example inputs reference publicly reported third-party data as of <span data-asof>November 17, 2026</span>; the sources named are not affiliated with, and have not endorsed, this tool. For terms that apply to your situation, speak with a licensed loan originator.</p>
          <p>Mountain State Financial Group, LLC · NMLS# 1314257 · Equal Housing Lender</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
